    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.statusline\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHello @echasnovski,\r\n\r\n[Using](https://github.com/abeldekat/nvim_pde/blob/7e487eadba39dbc91d458ab99c00e07c76028c79/lua/ak/config/ui/mini_statusline.lua#L27) this plugin I could dispose of many [lualine](https://github.com/abeldekat/nvim_pde/tree/cb35cae82bf13864f2e2254e915bcf807db959b6/lualine_themes/lua/lualine/themes) theme overrides. It was a joy to work with!\r\n\r\nI added diagnostic colors as described [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/337).\r\nIn order to do this, I also had to include code for the `lsp`(method `MiniStatusline.section_diagnostics`).\r\n\r\nCurrently, section `diagnostics` does not show when there is no [lsp](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/37d675dadeef2fad6aa4e7f12fde0f541a396cde/lua/mini/statusline.lua#L297) attached. Is that correct? The user could miss `diagnostics` when having a `linter` instead of an `lsp`.\r\n\r\nWould you accept a PR where the lsp string is created in a separate method?\r\nAn outline:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nH.default_content_active = function()\r\n...\r\n  local lsp   = MiniStatusline.section_lsp({ trunc_width = 75 }) --> new\r\n  local diagnostics   = MiniStatusline.section_diagnostics({ trunc_width = 75 })\r\n...\r\n  return MiniStatusline.combine_groups({\r\n...\r\n    { hl = 'MiniStatuslineDevinfo',  strings = { git, lsp, diagnostics } },\r\n...\r\n  })\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nBest regards!\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2024-05-23T07:59:56Z",
