    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n> Currently, section `diagnostics` does not show when there is no [lsp](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/37d675dadeef2fad6aa4e7f12fde0f541a396cde/lua/mini/statusline.lua#L297) attached. Is that correct? The user could miss `diagnostics` when having a `linter` instead of an `lsp`.\r\n\r\nOh, you are completely right! This somehow slipped past me when I implemented this.\r\n\r\nRight now, I don't particularly see much use in having separate `LSP` section (which would show server info, I presume?). Let me think about the possibly best way to resolve this. ",
