        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I have finally reached the first part of 'mini.statusline' refactor. The `section_diagnostics()` now depends exclusively on what data is returned by `vim.diagnostic.get()`. See [changelog entry](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#ministatusline) for more details.\r\n\r\nIt also means that the icon is not shown if there is no diagnostic entries in the buffer. Previously it served as an indicator that LSP server was attached to the buffer. Now there is a `section_lsp()` in default active content that serves this exact purpose.",
